  <h1>SimSD: Restoring Token-Level Speculative Decoding for Diffusion Language Models</h1>
  <p class="lead">Diffusion language models (dLLMs) decode text sequences in parallel using bidirectional attention. However, this bidirectional structure breaks the temporal context needed for speculative decoding. SimSD (UC San Diego, 2026) solves this with a training-free attention mask and data-mask layout that enables parallel token verification, unlocking up to a 7.46x throughput speedup.</p>
