<section id="s-bleed" data-code="bleed">
<div class="section-no">01 — Context Bleed</div>
<h2>The Temporal Context Collision</h2>
<p>Autoregressive (AR) models generate sequences strictly token-by-token. During verification in speculative decoding, this causal structure ensures that a target model can evaluate multiple drafted tokens in a single forward pass because the causal attention mask prevents future tokens from affecting past predictions.</p>

<p>In contrast, diffusion large language models (dLLMs) denoise sequences using <strong>bidirectional self-attention</strong>. Because they lack a causal mask, all positions attend to all other positions. During speculative decoding, if we simply feed the drafted tokens into a target dLLM, the bidirectional attention allows information from later draft tokens to bleed back into earlier positions. This alters the conditioning context and corrupts the computed logits, preventing parallel token verification.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">causal-vs-bidirectional-leakage.svg</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">why bidirectional attention breaks draft verification</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 680 180" style="width:100%;max-width:680px;display:block;margin:0 auto" font-family="var(--ff-mono)" font-size="10">
      <!-- Causal (AR) Speculative verification -->
      <text x="160" y="20" text-anchor="middle" fill="#a78bfa" font-weight="600">Autoregressive Causal Verification</text>
      
      <rect x="20" y="35" width="40" height="24" rx="4" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.1)" stroke="var(--purple)"/>
      <text x="40" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--text2)">[Le]</text>
      
      <rect x="80" y="35" width="40" height="24" rx="4" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.1)" stroke="var(--purple)"/>
      <text x="100" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--text2)">[chat]</text>
      
      <rect x="140" y="35" width="40" height="24" rx="4" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.15)" stroke="var(--purple)"/>
      <text x="160" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="#a78bfa" font-weight="600">[sur]</text>
      
      <rect x="200" y="35" width="40" height="24" rx="4" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.02)" stroke="var(--border-hi)"/>
      <text x="220" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)">[le]</text>

      <!-- Draw causal attention arrows -->
      <path d="M 40 59 C 40 75, 160 75, 160 59" fill="none" stroke="var(--purple)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
      <path d="M 100 59 C 100 70, 160 70, 160 59" fill="none" stroke="var(--purple)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
      <text x="100" y="78" font-size="7" fill="var(--purple-l)" text-anchor="middle">Only attends to prefix history</text>
      
      <line x1="340" y1="10" x2="340" y2="170" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1"/>

      <!-- Bidirectional leak -->
      <text x="500" y="20" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f472b6" font-weight="600">dLLM Bidirectional Leakage</text>
      
      <rect x="360" y="35" width="40" height="24" rx="4" fill="rgba(244,114,182,.1)" stroke="var(--border-hi)"/>
      <text x="380" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--text2)">[Le]</text>
      
