<section id="s-mask" data-code="mask">
<div class="section-no">03 — Temporal Causal Mask</div>
<h2>The Verification Flow Rules</h2>
<p>To enforce temporal prefix boundaries, we construct an attention mask $A_&#123;ij&#125;$ using temporal step labels $\tau(i) \in [1, \dots, \gamma]$, indicating when each token was generated. The rules governing visibility between any two response positions $i$ and $j$ are defined as:</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">SimSD Attention Visibility Matrix</div>
  A_ij = 1 iff:
  <br/>• i, j ∈ D <span class="math-comment"># Data reads Data: only past or same steps</span>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and <span class="math-var">τ(j) ≤ τ(i)</span>
  <br/>• i ∈ D, j ∈ \tilde&#123;D&#125; <span class="math-comment"># Data reads Mask: only future steps (unresolved contexts)</span>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and <span class="math-var">τ(j) &gt; τ(i)</span>
  <br/>• i ∈ \tilde&#123;D&#125;, j ∈ D <span class="math-comment"># Mask reads Data: only past steps (prefix context)</span>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and <span class="math-var">τ(j) &lt; τ(i)</span>
  <br/>• i, j ∈ \tilde&#123;D&#125; <span class="math-comment"># Mask reads Mask: only future or same steps</span>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and <span class="math-var">τ(j) ≥ τ(i)</span>
</div>

<p>Hover over the attention matrix below to see the visibility rules in action for each query row. Notice how the prompt is visible to all positions, and how each mask slot is isolated from future draft tokens.</p>

