</section>

<section id="s-verify" data-code="verify">
<div class="section-no">04 — Speculative Verification</div>
<h2>The Parallel Verification Walkthrough</h2>
<p>Once the sequence layout is prepared and the attention mask is constructed, the target model runs a **single forward pass**. Because the mask slots are causally isolated, the computed target logits represent valid prefix-conditioned distributions. We can then score and accept or reject all drafted tokens in parallel along the draft sequence order.</p>

<p>Use the step navigator below to step through a complete speculative verification block, showing how draft tokens are verified and how corrections are sampled when a rejection is encountered.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">speculative-verification-steps</span>
    <span class="vp-hint" id="step-prog">Step 1 of 5</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div class="step-list">
      <div class="step-box active">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Draft Proposal Generation</div>
          <div class="step-desc">A smaller draft dLLM proposes a sequence of candidate tokens (e.g. <code>["Le", "chat", "sur", "le"]</code>) and determines their temporal generation order.</div>
          <div class="step-code">draft_ids = draft_model.sample(context, steps=gamma)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Layout Synthesis & Position Alignment</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Duplicate the drafted sequence to build the Data-Mask paired layout, and copy position IDs from the Data section to the Mask section for positional consistency.</div>
          <div class="step-code">input_ids, pos_ids = prepare_layout(prompt_ids, draft_ids)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Target Model Forward Pass</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Run the target dLLM with the temporal causal attention mask. This evaluates prefix-conditioned logits for all mask slots in parallel.</div>
          <div class="step-code">target_logits = target_model(input_ids, position_ids, mask=simsd_mask)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Parallel Rejection Sampling</div>
          <div class="step-desc">For each drafted token, evaluate the acceptance probability: <code>α = min(1, p_target(x) / p_draft(x))</code>. The verification proceeds until the first rejection.</div>
          <div class="step-code">alpha = min(1.0, p_target / p_draft)</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">5</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Acceptance Commit & Backtracking</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Commit the accepted prefix tokens. If a token is rejected, sample a replacement from the corrected target distribution: <code>p_corr ∝ max(0, p_target - p_draft)</code>, and discard the rest of the draft.</div>
          <div class="step-code">commit(accepted_prefix) & resample_at_first_rejection()</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    
